        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. US-Iran peace negotiations abruptly called off amid growing criticism Middle East Issued on: 19/06/2026 - 11:05 Talks ⁠that had ​been planned for ​June 19 between the United States and Iran ⁠in Switzerland were abruptly called off, as the Trump administration faces mounting criticism from both Democrats and Republicans. This comes after Iran delayed sending its delegation to Switzerland over Israel’s ongoing military campaign in Lebanon. FRANCE 24's Douglas Herbert. Iran says Trump agreed to deal terms 'out of desperation' as US Democrats blast agreement 19/06/2026 Americas Replay: US VP JD Vance defends Iran-US agreement and FRANCE 24's analysis 18/06/2026 Middle East For Israel, US-Iran deal a 'disaster' incompatible with its security interests 18/06/2026 Middle East As a result of Iran war, Gulf states 'diversifying defensively' 18/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran agreement leaves Israelis 'in profound state of shock' 18/06/2026 Middle East Face-to-face signing of US-Iran deal 'up in the air' after Trump's Versailles signing 18/06/2026 Middle East Kept outside of negotiations, can the US-Iran deal bring peace to Lebanon? 18/06/2026 Middle East Tehran comes out as the 'winner' of the initial US - Iran deal 18/06/2026 Middle East 18/06/2026 Middle East"
